# Acta — Personal Evidence Graph Planning Context

Working brand: **Acta** (Latin *acta* — deeds / record of what was done). Project folder may still be `Stilva/` until renamed.

Canonical docs (`docs/`):

- `docs/personal-evidence-graph.md` — product spec (vision, wedge, adapters, monetization, relevance behavior)
- `docs/data-model.md` — data model / schema (entities, edges, captures, provenance). Own this separately; don't invent schema only in chat or only in the product doc.
- `docs/surfaces-and-flows.md` — IA / surfaces + core interaction flows
- `docs/agent-interaction-model.md` — agents, confirm vs auto, pending proposals, write policy
- `docs/graph-canvas.md` — the live spec for the graph canvas: hard requirements, what's deferred, and how we work on it (one verified slice at a time)
- `docs/building-plan.md` — build roadmap. **Units are `U-A`…`U-J`** (say “U-D”, never bare “D” for roadmap items). See Doc conventions in that file. **U-J** = technical implementation plan (HOW).
- `docs/design-handoff.md` — pixels on screen today (Neubrutalism, routes, chrome inventory)

When this conversation involves the graph canvas — physics, rendering, labels, zoom, drag, or how it should look and feel:

1. **Read/update `docs/graph-canvas.md`.** State requirements as things checkable on a running screen; don't re-specify a visual system in advance of building it.
2. **Build in slices and look at each one** before starting the next; front-end quality here is not one-shottable. `src/styles/tokens.css` remains the token source of truth.
3. Don't reintroduce the archived "liquid glass" translucency over live content — text over the moving graph goes on opaque surfaces for now.

When this conversation involves product vision, scope, wedge, relevance, capture, competitive landscape, positioning, or open product questions:

1. **Read** `docs/personal-evidence-graph.md` before planning or advising if it isn't already in context.
2. **Update** that doc when decisions change, new open questions appear, questions get resolved, scope shifts, or important insights land — don't leave planning only in chat.

When this conversation involves schema, entity types, edges, extraction contracts, dedup, provenance storage, or capture↔entity relationships:

1. **Read/update `docs/data-model.md`** as the source of truth for those decisions.
2. Keep `docs/personal-evidence-graph.md` in sync only at the summary/lean level (link out; don't duplicate full schema).

When this conversation involves agents, tools, confirm vs auto, pending proposals, or what systems may write to the graph:

1. **Read/update `docs/agent-interaction-model.md`** as the source of truth for write policy.
2. Keep extract emit shapes and stamp rules in `docs/data-model.md`; keep chrome in `docs/surfaces-and-flows.md`.

General:

- Prefer editing existing sections over duplicating; bump "Last updated" and add a short Changelog entry.
- Do not invent settled decisions; if unsure, add an open question instead.
- Product spec altitude: capture what/why/scope; defer detailed UI/UX/flows unless asked.
- When referring to building-plan workstreams, always use **U-A**, **U-B**, **U-C**, … through **U-J** (never bare A/B/C for those units).
